00:38:06.500 --> 00:38:28.980
<v Sean Cole>It's This American Life. And I'm Sean Cole in for Ira Glass. Today's show-- Seeing Yourself in the Wild, stories of people who get to-- reluctantly decide to-- come face to face with an unedited version of who they are and what they do with that information. And I am now delighted to bring you Act 2 of our show. Act 2, distant replay.
<v Sean Cole>这里是《美国生活》。我是肖恩·科尔，代替艾拉·格拉斯主持。今天的节目——“在野外看到你自己”，讲述人们如何不得不——很不情愿地决定——去面对他们是谁的未剪辑版本，以及他们如何处理这些信息。我现在很高兴给你们带来我们节目的第二幕。第二幕，远距离重放。

00:38:28.980 --> 00:38:47.910
<v Sean Cole>So, this story is about a man who's been reliving this one moment from his life over and over again. He remembers every last detail of how it felt, how it changed his life. And then 40 years later, someone shows up with a recording of that thing. Emanuele Berry explains.
<v Sean Cole>所以，这个故事关于一个男人，他一直在一遍又一遍地重温他生活中的那一刻。他记得那种感觉的每一个细节，它是如何改变了他的人生。然后40年后，有人带着那个东西的录音出现了。埃马努埃莱·贝里为您讲述。

00:38:47.910 --> 00:39:16.570
<v Emanuele Berry>The man is my dad. And the thing he cannot let go of is a high school basketball game from 1978. I found out about the game when I was a kid. My mom had saved this old newspaper clipping, or maybe it was a yearbook. But either way, there is this picture of my dad on a basketball court. And when I brought it to her, she told me not to ask my dad about it. And so, I never brought it up. But it bugged me, because basketball is the one thing my dad and I share.
<v Emanuele Berry>那个男人是我爸爸。他无法放下的是1978年的一场高中篮球赛。我小时候发现了那场比赛。我妈妈留着那张旧报纸剪报，或者可能是毕业纪念册。但无论如何，照片里是我爸爸在篮球场上。当我把它拿给她看时，她告诉我不要问我爸爸关于它的事。所以，我从没提起过。但这一直困扰着我，因为篮球是我和我爸爸共同拥有的东西。

00:39:16.570 --> 00:39:54.370
<v Emanuele Berry>Of my four siblings, I'm the only one who fell for the game like my dad. I loved being on the court; the sound of squeaking shoes, creaking floors; the way the entire space of the gym would vibrate; the way my body would twist, and turn, and pivot to the basket. I loved basketball, but I also loved the attention my dad gave me because of it. In the car after games, we'd annoy the hell out of the rest of my family by dissecting my every move, figuring out what I could improve on, what I did well. It was like we were speaking our own language. Together, we laid out big dreams for my future-- club teams, high school star, college, the WNBA.
<v Emanuele Berry>在四个兄弟姐妹中，我是唯一一个像我爸爸一样迷上这项运动的人。我喜欢在球场上的感觉；球鞋摩擦声，地板吱吱声；整个体育馆空间都在震动的感觉；我的身体为了投篮而扭转、旋转和转向的方式。我热爱篮球，但我也热爱我爸爸因此而给我的关注。比赛后的车里，我们会通过剖析我的每一个动作，弄清楚我能改进什么，做得好的地方，来烦死我们家庭里的其他人。感觉我们是在说我们自己的语言。我们一起为我的未来规划了宏伟的梦想——俱乐部球队、高中明星、大学、WNBA。

00:39:54.370 --> 00:40:06.410
<v Emanuele Berry>But when I got to high school, I cared less about the game. Our postgame talk stopped feeling like conversations and started sounding like lectures. I started to dread the car rides home.
<v Emanuele Berry>但我到了高中时，我不再那么关心比赛了。我们的赛后谈话不再像是对话，而听起来像是讲座。我开始害怕回家的车程。

00:40:06.410 --> 00:40:30.690
<v Emanuele Berry>And there's one ride for my junior year of high school that I still think about all the time. I was walking to my dad's car after the game. And as soon as I closed the door, it started. Why didn't you do this? You need to do this. How could you do this? As I listen to the steady rhythm of my dad's critique, I realized, these lectures weren't about me or what I wanted. They were about him.
<v Emanuele Berry>我高二时有一次回家的车程，我一直还在想。比赛后我正走向我爸爸的车。我刚关上车门，就开始了。“为什么你不做这个？”“你需要做那个。”“你怎么能做那个？”当我听着爸爸批评的稳定节奏，我意识到，这些讲座不是关于我或者我想要的。它们是关于他自己的。

00:40:30.690 --> 00:41:00.890
<v Emanuele Berry>So I did something I had never done before. Shut the fuck up, I shouted. He was taken aback for a moment, and then stony silence, waiting for an apology. But it was an apology I wouldn't give. I told him that I didn't want to talk about basketball with him anymore. And if that's all he wanted to talk about, we didn't need to talk. So we didn't. For over a year, we barely spoke to each other.
<v Emanuele Berry>所以我做了我以前从未做过的事。“他妈的闭嘴，”我喊道。他愣了一会儿，然后是死一样的沉默，等着道歉。但我绝不会道歉。我告诉他我不想再跟他谈论篮球了。如果那是他唯一想谈的话题，那我们就不必谈了。所以我们没谈。一年多来，我们几乎没说过话。

00:41:00.890 --> 00:41:19.570
<v Emanuele Berry>A lot of time has passed. I haven't picked up a ball in forever. Neither has my dad. The silence is long gone. But there's something that hasn't been repaired. Nowadays, we just exchange basketball pleasantries. Did you watch that game? How does the team look this year? LeBron, LeBron, LeBron.
<v Emanuele Berry>时间过去很久了。我很久没碰过球了。我爸爸也没碰过。沉默早就消失了。但有些事情还没修复。如今，我们只是交换篮球客套话。“你看那场比赛了吗？”“球队今年看起来怎么样？”“勒布朗，勒布朗，勒布朗。”

00:41:19.570 --> 00:41:40.600
<v Emanuele Berry>Basketball gives us the illusion that we know each other. But I'm not sure we do. And I've been wanting to know my dad better-- to talk to him about something real, something that matters to him. So that high school basketball game from 1978 seems like a good place to start.
<v Emanuele Berry>篮球给了我们一种我们了解彼此的错觉。但我并不确定我们真的了解。我一直想更了解我爸爸——和他谈论一些真实的事情，一些对他来说重要的事情。所以那场1978年的高中篮球赛似乎是个很好的起点。

00:41:40.600 --> 00:42:00.160
<v Emanuele Berry>I visited my parents in Michigan. And when I walk into the living room, of course, there's a college basketball game on in the background. My dad's in his usual position, sunken into his recliner. Even sitting down, he's still big. Long arms-- his hands make the remote look teeny. I ask him to talk upstairs.
<v Emanuele Berry>我去了密歇根看望我父母。当我走进客厅时，当然，背景里正播放着一场大学篮球赛。我爸爸在他通常的位置，陷在他的躺椅里。即使坐着，他依然庞大。长长的手臂——他的手让遥控器看起来微不足道。我让他上楼聊聊。

00:42:00.160 --> 00:42:00.840
<v Bobby Berry>On what?
<v Bobby Berry>聊什么？

00:42:00.840 --> 00:42:02.780
<v Emanuele Berry>Do you want to sit back here?
<v Emanuele Berry>你想坐在后面吗？

00:42:02.780 --> 00:42:04.030
<v Bobby Berry>Anywhere is OK with me.
<v Bobby Berry>在哪儿都行。

00:42:04.030 --> 00:42:04.800
<v Emanuele Berry>OK.
<v Emanuele Berry>好吧。

00:42:04.800 --> 00:42:05.660
<v Bobby Berry>I go to sleep.
<v Bobby Berry>我去睡觉了。

00:42:05.660 --> 00:42:08.210
<v Emanuele Berry>No, you can't go to sleep. We're talking.
<v Emanuele Berry>不，你不能去睡觉。我们在聊天。

00:42:08.210 --> 00:42:16.430
<v Sean Cole>I'm nervous. My dad is intimidating. We chit chat for a long time before I bring up the game and that old photo my mom had kept.
<v Sean Cole>我很紧张。我爸爸很有威慑力。在提起那场比赛和我妈妈保留的那张旧照片之前，我们聊了很久。

00:42:16.430 --> 00:42:23.090
<v Emanuel Berry>And I remember her saying that it was sad and that I shouldn't mention it.
<v Emanuel Berry>我还记得她说那很伤感，我不该提它。

00:42:23.090 --> 00:42:32.130
<v Bobby Berry>That picture was of the final game when we lost in the semifinals. I blame myself for losing that game.
<v Bobby Berry>那张照片是我们在半决赛输掉的最后一场比赛。我自责输了那场球。

00:42:32.130 --> 00:42:35.480
<v Emanuele Berry>Why?
<v Emanuele Berry>为什么？

00:42:35.480 --> 00:42:42.480
<v Emanuele Berry>[DEEP SIGH]
<v Emanuele Berry>[深呼吸]

00:42:42.480 --> 00:42:57.260
<v Sean Cole>There's a lot in that sigh. My dad grew up poor in Mississippi, the youngest of 11. And for him, basketball was a way to college. But in the 10th grade, he suffered a serious knee injury. His knee would swell when he ran, so he had to stop playing.
<v Sean Cole>那个叹息里包含了很多。我爸爸在密西西比贫困长大，是11个孩子里最小的。对他来说，篮球是上大学的一条路。但在高一的时候，他遭遇了严重的膝伤。他跑步时膝盖会肿胀，所以不得不停止打球。

00:42:57.260 --> 00:43:18.060
<v Sean Cole>But he got an unlikely second chance. Before his senior year of high school, his family moved to Michigan. There, the surgeon found bone shards under my dad's kneecap. He removed them, and the swelling stopped. My dad could play basketball again. That dream to get a basketball scholarship to go to college was back on.
<v Sean Cole>但他得到了一个不太可能的第二次机会。高三前夕，他全家搬到了密歇根。在那里，外科医生发现我爸爸的髌骨下有骨碎片。他移除了它们，肿胀消失了。我爸爸又能打篮球了。那个获得篮球奖学金上大学的梦想又回来了。

00:43:18.060 --> 00:43:46.230
<v Sean Cole>My dad joined his high school basketball team. They were called the Everett Vikings, and they were good. They'd won the state championship the previous year. The star of that team was this guy named Earvin. But most people just call him Magic Johnson. Even in high school, they called them that. The coach was thrilled when my dad joined because he was tall. And the team had lost Magic Johnson and all of their height. As the season progressed, my dad flourished. He was a strong rebounder. He could dunk. He even got a nickname.
<v Sean Cole>我爸爸加入了他的高中篮球队。他们叫埃弗雷特维京队，他们很棒。他们前一年赢得了州冠军。那支球队的明星是一个叫厄文的家伙。但大多数人只是叫他“魔术师”约翰逊。甚至在高中时，他们就这么叫他。教练很兴奋，因为我爸爸加入了，他很高。而球队失去了“魔术师”约翰逊和他们所有的身高优势。随着赛季的推进，我爸爸风生水起。他是一个强大的篮板手。他会扣篮。他甚至得了个外号。

00:43:46.230 --> 00:44:08.930
<v Bobby Berry>They wanted to try to figure out a name for me, a nickname for me. They already had one for Earvin. As everybody know, Tim Scott nicknamed Earvin "Magic" Johnson. One of the sportscasters found out I was from Mississippi. During a game where I dunked the ball, he said, Mississippi Slammer. That's where they got the name the Mississippi Slammer.
<v Bobby Berry>他们想给我起个名字，一个外号。他们已经给厄文起了一个。正如每个人所知，蒂姆·斯科特给厄文起了“魔术师”约翰逊这个绰号。其中一个体育播音员发现我来自密西西比。在一场我扣篮的比赛中，他说：“密西西比重击者。”他们就是从那儿得来的“密西西比重击者”这个外号。

00:44:08.930 --> 00:44:23.240
<v Emanuele Berry>His team was cruising through the season to the state playoffs, which brings us to the game I was never supposed to ask about. It was the semifinals. The team was supposed to wear suits to the game, but my dad didn't have one. So he had to get one at the last minute.
<v Emanuele Berry>他的球队在赛季中高歌猛进，进入了州季后赛，这就带到了我本不该问的那场比赛。那是半决赛。球队本该穿西装去参加比赛，但我爸爸没有。所以他不得不在最后一分钟找了一套。

00:44:23.240 --> 00:44:38.500
<v Emanuele Berry>He missed the pep rally, and he got to the gym late. My dad remembers going to the locker room, the starting lineups being announced. And when the game started, he says he just felt off. He remembers this one play in particular, where he says everything fell apart.
<v Emanuele Berry>他错过了动员大会，迟到了体育馆。我爸爸记得走进更衣室，首发阵容被宣布。比赛开始时，他说他感觉很不对劲。他记得特别是在那次进攻中，他说一切都崩盘了。

00:44:38.500 --> 00:45:12.830
<v Bobby Berry>I grab a rebound off the backboard above the rim. And I go up above the rim, to where I'm basically-- all I had to do was just drop the ball in the basket. Instead, I threw it across the basket. And I never will forget it. It was hard on me because that was a turning point in the game that had made me feel that I lost the game.
<v Bobby Berry>我从篮圈上方的篮板抢下一个篮板。我跳到篮圈上方，基本上——我唯一要做的就是把球投进篮筐。相反，我把球扔过了篮圈。我永远不会忘记它。这对我来说很艰难，因为那是比赛的一个转折点，让我觉得是我输掉了比赛。

00:45:12.830 --> 00:45:16.500
<v Emanuele Berry>How long do you think you carried around that one little moment?
<v Emanuele Berry>你觉得你把那一个小瞬间携带了多久？

00:45:16.500 --> 00:45:22.740
<v Bobby Berry>I still carry it around. Obviously, I'm still talking about it.
<v Bobby Berry>我还在携带它。显然，我还在谈论它。

00:45:22.740 --> 00:45:27.940
<v Emanuele Berry>What do you think would make you not carry it around with you?
<v Emanuele Berry>你认为什么会让你不再携带它？

00:45:27.940 --> 00:45:33.800
<v Bobby Berry>I don't know. I can't go back in time and redo it.
<v Bobby Berry>我不知道。我不能回到过去重做一次。

00:45:33.800 --> 00:45:36.730
<v Emanuele Berry>They lost the game by just a few points.
<v Emanuele Berry>他们以几分的优势输掉了比赛。

00:45:36.730 --> 00:45:40.600
<v Emanuele Berry>Did it feel like opportunities were closing for you with that game?
<v Emanuele Berry>那场比赛让你感觉机会在关闭吗？

00:45:40.600 --> 00:46:29.640
<v Bobby Berry>Yeah. If I had played better, and we would've won that game, we would have been in the finals. And there would've been more visual eyes on us. And the thing was is that I was only out there for one year because I came up here in my senior year. So nobody really knew who I was. For me to get the more exposure, we needed to continue to win. And when we didn't win, I think that just-- a lot of the opportunities for me to be seen went out the window. I have a lot of resentment about the opportunities that I feel that it could have changed my life from the way we are now.
<v Bobby Berry>是的。如果我打得更好，我们会赢得那场比赛，我们就会进入决赛。那样会有更多的视觉关注到我们身上。问题是我只打了一年，因为我高三才来到这里。所以没人真正知道我是谁。为了获得更多的曝光，我们需要继续赢。当我们没赢时，我想那只是——我觉得很多本可以改变我人生的机会就这样溜走了。对于我觉得本可以改变我们现在这种生活的机会，我有很多怨恨。

00:46:29.640 --> 00:46:55.460
<v Emanuele Berry>When my dad says where we are now, he means no college degree, a career managing restaurants, raising five kids, and making ends meet. Where we are now is missing part of a lung and slipped discs. Where we are now is no kidneys and dialysis, while still working 60 hour weeks. It's been over 40 years since he missed that shot. Maybe that's how long it takes to mourn an alternative universe.
<v Emanuele Berry>当我爸爸说“我们现在这种生活”时，他指的是没有大学学位，做着餐厅管理，抚养五个孩子，勉强维持生计。我们现在所处的地方是肺部缺失了一部分和椎间盘突出。我们现在所处的地方是没有肾脏和透析，同时还要每周工作60小时。他错过那次投篮已经40多年了。也许这就是哀悼平行宇宙所需要的时间。

00:46:55.460 --> 00:47:16.710
<v Emanuele Berry>But part of me also wonders, isn't that long enough to let it go-- to see that it's just a game? That where we are now is also 40 years of marriage and kids who went to college, one even to Yale-- not me. And it's not like my dad hates his job. I've never thought of our life as anything other than a good one.
<v Emanuele Berry>但我的一部分也在怀疑，这不是够长了吗，足以让它过去——看到那只是场比赛？“我们现在所处的地方”也是40年的婚姻和上了大学的孩子，甚至有一个上了耶鲁——不是我。而且并不是我爸爸讨厌他的工作。我从未认为我们的生活有任何不如意。

00:47:16.710 --> 00:47:28.920
<v Emanuele Berry>I got it in my head that if he could watch the game, he'd see things differently. Maybe he didn't play so badly. Maybe he's just being hard on himself. And I wanted to see it. I've never seen him play.
<v Emanuele Berry>我脑子里产生了一个想法，如果他能看那场比赛，他会以不同的方式看待事情。也许他并没打得那么糟。也许他只是对自己太苛刻了。我想看那场比赛。我从没见过他打球。

00:47:28.920 --> 00:47:55.100
<v Emanuele Berry>So I looked for the tape everywhere-- his high school, TV stations, the Michigan High School Athletic Association. And then, a few months later, my dad reconnected with one of his high school teammates. And he said, I have a copy of the game. And not only that, but he and the other guys on the team had a different take of how my dad played. They said they remembered him playing great-- that he's the reason they even stayed in the game.
<v Emanuele Berry>所以我到处寻找录像带——他的高中、电视台、密歇根州高中体育协会。然后，几个月后，我爸爸联系上了他的一位高中队友。他说：“我有一份比赛录像。”不仅如此，他和球队的其他家伙对我的打球方式有不同的看法。他们说他们记得他打得很棒——他是他们留在比赛中的原因。

00:47:55.100 --> 00:48:06.270
<v Emanuele Berry>He gave the tape to my dad. My dad tried to watch it once, but didn't get too far. So, a few weeks ago, we sat down in the living room to watch the game together.
<v Emanuele Berry>他把录像带给了我爸爸。我爸爸试着看了一次，但没看太久。所以，几周前，我们坐在客厅一起看比赛。

00:48:06.270 --> 00:48:08.430
<v Emanuele Berry>All right, you ready?
<v Emanuele Berry>好了，准备好了吗？

00:48:08.430 --> 00:48:09.330
<v Bobby Berry>I think so.
<v Bobby Berry>我想是吧。

00:48:09.330 --> 00:48:12.670
<v Emanuele Berry>You think so? Are you worried right now?
<v Emanuele Berry>你觉得是吧？你现在担心吗？

00:48:12.670 --> 00:48:13.960
<v Bobby Berry>I'm nervous.
<v Bobby Berry>我很紧张。

00:48:13.960 --> 00:48:16.560
<v Emanuele Berry>Why? What are you nervous about?
<v Emanuele Berry>为什么？你担心什么？

00:48:16.560 --> 00:48:50.000
<v Bobby Berry>Watching myself 40 years ago playing basketball, revisiting those moments. But my teammates said that I played very like a bear, or beast, or whatever. I would like to see that part of the video. Versus what I perceive that I did not play very well. So from retrospective, I would like to see that version-- the beast.
<v Bobby Berry>看着40年前打球的自己，重温那些时刻。但我队友说我打得像头熊，或者野兽，或者别的什么。我想看录像的那部分。相比我所感知到的我没打好。所以从回顾的角度看，我想看那个版本——野兽。

00:48:50.000 --> 00:48:52.270
<v Emanuele Berry>The beast? The Mississippi Slammer?
<v Emanuele Berry>野兽？密西西比重击者？

00:48:52.270 --> 00:48:56.210
<v Bobby Berry>Well, you know, I'd take anything right now.
<v Bobby Berry>好吧，你知道，我现在什么都能接受。

00:48:56.210 --> 00:48:58.660
<v Emanuele Berry>Here we go.
<v Emanuele Berry>我们开始了。

00:48:58.660 --> 00:49:06.280
<v Sean Cole>A grainy black and white court comes into focus. Players zoomed towards the basket and layup lines. Lots of them have afros.
<v Sean Cole>一个颗粒状的黑白球场进入视线。球员们在篮筐和上篮线上来回穿梭。他们中很多人留着爆炸头。

00:49:06.280 --> 00:49:08.920
<v Bobby Berry>Can you tell which one is me?
<v Bobby Berry>你能看出来哪个是我吗？

00:49:08.920 --> 00:49:12.940
<v Emanuele Berry>Um, not yet. Well, it's all over the place.
<v Emanuele Berry>嗯，还没。好吧，到处都是。

00:49:12.940 --> 00:49:18.860
<v Sean Cole>And then I see him. It's his body language, so like my little brother's that it gives him away.
<v Sean Cole>然后我看到了他。那是他的肢体语言，和我弟弟的太像了，直接暴露了他。

00:49:18.860 --> 00:49:19.460
<v Emanuele Berry>Is this you?
<v Emanuele Berry>这是你吗？

00:49:19.460 --> 00:49:20.090
<v Bobby Berry>That's me, yeah.
<v Bobby Berry>那是我是的。

00:49:20.090 --> 00:49:20.870
<v Emanuele Berry>Is that you?
<v Emanuele Berry>那是你吗？

00:49:20.870 --> 00:49:22.400
<v Bobby Berry>Yes, that's me.
<v Bobby Berry>是的，是我。

00:49:22.400 --> 00:49:37.370
<v Emanuele Berry>He's sporting a white jersey and teeny, tight white shorts that are very shy of his knees. Tube socks and high top sneakers-- the shoes make me cringe. Ankle support apparently was not a thing. And he's way skinnier than I've ever known him.
<v Emanuele Berry>他穿着一件白色球衣，紧身的白色短裤离膝盖很远。筒袜和高帮球鞋——这些鞋让我觉得局促。踝关节支撑显然当时不是个事儿。他比我认识的任何时候都要瘦得多。

00:49:37.370 --> 00:49:37.910
<v Emanuele Berry>You're so teeny.
<v Emanuele Berry>你太苗条了。

00:49:37.910 --> 00:49:40.770
<v Emanuele Berry>[LAUGHTER]
<v Emanuele Berry>[笑声]

00:49:40.770 --> 00:49:44.680
<v Bobby Berry>Yeah, all 189 pounds of me.
<v Bobby Berry>是的，我当时189磅重。

00:49:44.680 --> 00:49:46.480
<v Emanuele Berry>When was the last time you were 189 pounds.
<v Emanuele Berry>你上一次189磅是什么时候。

00:49:46.480 --> 00:49:50.610
<v Bobby Berry>Yeah, in high school.
<v Bobby Berry>是啊，在高中时。

00:49:50.610 --> 00:49:53.000
<v TV Announcer>Hold on, this game is underway.
<v TV Announcer>等等，比赛开始了。

00:49:53.000 --> 00:50:07.490
<v Emanuele Berry>The teams line up at the big [INAUDIBLE] half court for the jump ball. My dad loses the jump. The other team picks the ball up on the court, fires off a quick jumper that bounces off the rim. My dad's team takes the ball down, and throws up a shot, and also misses. My dad grabs the rebound.
<v Emanuele Berry>两队在半场争球。我爸爸丢了那个球。对方球队捡起球，投出一个快速跳投，弹框而出。我爸爸的球队带球下底，投篮，也投失了。我爸爸抢下篮板。

00:50:07.490 --> 00:50:09.170
<v TV Announcer>Bobby Berry has it.
<v TV Announcer>鲍比·贝里拿到了球。

00:50:09.170 --> 00:50:19.610
<v Emanuele Berry>Bobby Berry-- that's my dad. The funny thing is that as he watches, he seems to forget that he knows how this game ends. And he's watching it like any other game on TV.
<v Emanuele Berry>鲍比·贝里——那是我爸爸。有趣的是，当他看着的时候，他似乎忘记了他知道这场比赛的结局。他像看电视上的任何其他比赛一样看着它。

00:50:19.610 --> 00:50:21.170
<v Bobby Berry>Come on.
<v Bobby Berry>来吧。

00:50:21.170 --> 00:50:29.840
<v Emanuele Berry>My dad's team scores the first two baskets. It's 4-0. But the lead doesn't seem to matter to him. He's already down on himself.
<v Emanuele Berry>我爸爸的球队进了前两个球。4-0。但领先对他来说似乎并不重要。他已经对自己很失望了。

00:50:29.840 --> 00:50:31.370
<v Emanuele Berry>What are you seeing right now?
<v Emanuele Berry>你现在看到了什么？

00:50:31.370 --> 00:50:33.230
<v Bobby Berry>Me standing.
<v Bobby Berry>我站在那儿。

00:50:33.230 --> 00:50:34.160
<v Emanuele Berry>Yeah?
<v Emanuele Berry>是吗？

00:50:34.160 --> 00:50:35.150
<v Bobby Berry>Yep.
<v Bobby Berry>是的。

00:50:35.150 --> 00:50:36.180
<v Emanuele Berry>What do you mean?
<v Emanuele Berry>什么意思？

00:50:36.180 --> 00:50:44.600
<v Bobby Berry>Um, I don't go to the ball. I go away from the ball. Watch the ball come to this side. Now watch where I go-- opposite side of the ball.
<v Bobby Berry>嗯，我不去抢球。我远离球。看球来到这一侧。现在看我去了哪儿——球的另一侧。

00:50:44.600 --> 00:50:50.650
<v Emanuele Berry>I start to say things like, it just started. It's not that bad. I'm pointing out every good thing he does.
<v Emanuele Berry>我开始说类似“这刚开始而已。没那么糟。”我指出他做的每一件好事。

00:50:50.650 --> 00:50:52.710
<v Emanuele Berry>Look, you just got an offensive rebound.
<v Emanuele Berry>看，你刚拿了个进攻篮板。

00:50:52.710 --> 00:50:57.230
<v Sean Cole>And I'm so busy talking, I almost miss the play that's haunted my dad.
<v Sean Cole>我太忙于说话了，差点错过了缠绕我爸爸的那次进攻。

00:50:57.230 --> 00:51:01.320
<v TV Announcer>[INAUDIBLE] Tony Daniel high post drives around his hand, puts it up-- no good.
<v TV Announcer>[听不清] 托尼·丹尼尔高位运球，绕过他的手，投篮——没进。

00:51:01.320 --> 00:51:03.890
<v Emanuele Berry>You got the board.
<v Emanuele Berry>你拿到球了。

00:51:03.890 --> 00:51:04.340
<v Bobby Berry>There it is.
<v Bobby Berry>就是那个。

00:51:04.340 --> 00:51:07.580
<v Emanuele Berry>Is that the shot? Was that it?
<v Emanuele Berry>那是投篮吗？是那个吗？

00:51:07.580 --> 00:51:14.960
<v Bobby Berry>Yes. Yeah, that was the shot.
<v Bobby Berry>是的。是啊，那是那次投篮。

00:51:14.960 --> 00:51:15.500
<v Emanuele Berry>You want to--
<v Emanuele Berry>你想——

00:51:15.500 --> 00:51:23.080
<v Bobby Berry>[INAUDIBLE] No, I don't want to see it again. Once is enough.
<v Bobby Berry>[听不清] 不，我不想再看一遍。看一次就够了。

00:51:23.080 --> 00:51:36.230
<v Emanuele Berry>The play is over so quick. It's just a second on the screen. And the thing is after that shot, his teammate rebounds the ball and puts it in. In other words, the miss-- it didn't matter. They still score.
<v Emanuele Berry>进攻很快就结束了。屏幕上只有一秒钟。关键是那次投篮后，他的队友抢下篮板投进了。换句话说，投失了——这没关系。他们还是得分了。

00:51:36.230 --> 00:51:57.480
<v Emanuele Berry>But it did matter to my dad. He never really recovers. And for the rest of the game, he misses shot after shot. Though it's not all bad. He makes a monster block on the next play. Though watching, he barely seems to notice. Next play down, he's fouled on the shot. So he gets two free throws.
<v Emanuele Berry>但这对我爸爸有关系。他从没真正恢复过来。在比赛余下的时间里，他一次又一次投失。虽然也不全是坏事。他在接下来的进攻中做了一次怪物级的盖帽。虽然看着，他几乎没注意到。下一次进攻，他投篮被犯规了。所以他得到了两次罚球。

00:51:57.480 --> 00:52:02.340
<v Bobby Berry>Yeah, free throws! That's what I mean.
<v Bobby Berry>是啊，罚球！我就是这个意思。

00:52:02.340 --> 00:52:03.700
<v Emanuele Berry>You made your free throw.
<v Emanuele Berry>你罚进了。

00:52:03.700 --> 00:52:09.120
<v Bobby Berry>I missed a shot, two feet away.
<v Bobby Berry>我投失了一个两英尺外的球。

00:52:09.120 --> 00:52:13.270
<v Emanuele Berry>I keep trying to get him to see what his teammates saw. He won't.
<v Emanuele Berry>我一直试图让他看到他队友看到的东西。他不肯。

00:52:13.270 --> 00:52:15.420
<v Emanuele Berry>You guys are up by quite a bit.
<v Emanuele Berry>你们领先不少。

00:52:15.420 --> 00:52:23.870
<v Bobby Berry>Yeah, I know. That's the point. We lost.
<v Bobby Berry>是啊，我知道。重点是。我们输了。

00:52:23.870 --> 00:52:38.990
<v Emanuele Berry>At halftime, it's 22-21. My dad's team is up by one. But by the second half, it's as if my dad remembers what he's watching and how it ends. No more yelling, he just sort of sits hand over mouth, quiet.
<v Emanuele Berry>中场休息时，比分是22-21。我爸爸的球队领先一分。但到了下半场，似乎我爸爸记起了他在看什么以及它是如何结束的。不再大喊，他只是捂着嘴坐着，安静。

00:52:38.990 --> 00:52:59.270
<v Emanuele Berry>And this is where I start to think, wait, is he mad at me? I start to worry that this was a terrible idea. This isn't going to make him feel better. Rather than think about one mistake in a game from 40 years ago, he can now watch 40 minutes of mistakes.
<v Emanuele Berry>这时我开始想，等等，他在生我气吗？我开始担心这是个糟糕的主意。这不会让他感觉更好。与其思考40年前一场比赛中的一次错误，他现在可以看40分钟的错误。

00:52:59.270 --> 00:53:22.670
<v Emanuele Berry>The game remains close. And I can see what his teammates are saying about him being a beast. He's pulling down lots of rebounds. He is the reason they're still in the game. But he's not scoring much. Then, in the fourth quarter, their opponent pulls ahead by just a few. And my dad's team can't catch up. It's over.
<v Emanuele Berry>比赛依然胶着。我能看到他队友说的关于他是野兽的话。他摘下很多篮板。他是他们依然留在比赛中的原因。但他得分不多。然后，在第四节，他们的对手领先了几分。我爸爸的球队追不上。结束了。

00:53:22.670 --> 00:53:37.400
<v Emanuele Berry>The camera shows one final moment of my dad. It zooms in on him before he heads into the locker room. He leans down, wrapping his arms around his coach, consoling him. My father at the kitchen table has far less compassion for himself.
<v Emanuele Berry>摄像机记录了我爸爸的一个最后瞬间。在进入更衣室之前，镜头聚焦在他身上。他弯下腰，双臂搂着他的教练，安慰他。厨房桌前的我父亲对自己却缺乏同情心。

00:53:37.400 --> 00:53:39.630
<v Emanuele Berry>How are you feeling?
<v Emanuele Berry>你感觉怎么样？

00:53:39.630 --> 00:54:02.780
<v Bobby Berry>Uh, depressed. But I can't do anything about it. It's like I said. It's sad to see that game over again, that's for sure. And I didn't-- still, I feel the same way. I felt that I did not play very well, the way I felt that I should.
<v Bobby Berry>呃，沮丧。但我无能为力。就像我说的。看到那场比赛再次结束，真是令人伤心，这是肯定的。我没——依然，我感觉一样。我觉得我没打好，我觉得我本该打好的那种方式。

00:54:02.780 --> 00:54:09.420
<v Emanuele Berry>My dad finally got to see how this moment actually looked from the outside. And it didn't change anything for him.
<v Emanuele Berry>我爸爸终于看到了那一刻从外部看起来是什么样。这对他来说并没有改变什么。

00:54:09.420 --> 00:54:17.540
<v Bobby Berry>You can't imagine that things were different. The tape proves the way I felt that I played is what the tape shows.
<v Bobby Berry>你无法想象事情本可以不同。录像带证明我感觉我打球的方式就是录像带显示的。

00:54:17.540 --> 00:54:22.340
<v Emanuele Berry>When we were watching, I worried that I'd upset my dad. I had.
<v Emanuele Berry>我们看的时候，我担心我惹我不爸爸不高兴了。我的确惹了。

00:54:22.340 --> 00:54:24.140
<v Bobby Berry>Well, you're reopening a wound.
<v Bobby Berry>好吧，你重新打开了一个伤口。

00:54:24.140 --> 00:54:24.980
<v Emanuele Berry>Me?
<v Emanuele Berry>我？

00:54:24.980 --> 00:54:27.710
<v Bobby Berry>Yes. Why are you making me watch this game?
<v Bobby Berry>是的。为什么要让我看这场比赛？

00:54:27.710 --> 00:54:29.780
<v Emanuele Berry>Does it make you that upset?
<v Emanuele Berry>让你那么沮丧吗？

00:54:29.780 --> 00:54:34.190
<v Bobby Berry>I'm not upset. It just reopens it, and making me revisit it is not necessarily making me--
<v Bobby Berry>我不沮丧。它只是重新打开了它，让我重温它并不一定让我——

00:54:34.190 --> 00:54:41.480
<v Emanuele Berry>See, I think my hope was that by watching it, it would make you feel better. Like, you could let go of it.
<v Emanuele Berry>看，我认为我的希望是，通过看它，它会让你感觉更好。就像，你可以放下它。

00:54:41.480 --> 00:54:47.150
<v Bobby Berry>The only way I probably can ever let go of it is go back into time and reverse everything. And that's not going to happen.
<v Bobby Berry>我唯一能放下它的方法大概是回到过去改变一切。那是不可能发生的。

00:54:47.150 --> 00:54:48.310
<v Emanuele Berry>Is that really what it would take?
<v Emanuele Berry>真的需要那样才能放下吗？

00:54:48.310 --> 00:54:50.960
<v Bobby Berry>I think that's probably what it would take.
<v Bobby Berry>我想那大概就是所需要的。

00:54:50.960 --> 00:55:00.910
<v Emanuele Berry>I think it makes me upset that you feel upset or that you feel depressed about this. Because it just--
<v Emanuele Berry>我觉得你感到沮丧或者为这件事感到抑郁让我很难过。因为这只是——

00:55:00.910 --> 00:55:02.120
<v Bobby Berry>I know it's just a game.
<v Bobby Berry>我知道这只是场比赛。

00:55:02.120 --> 00:55:07.350
<v Emanuele Berry>It's not that it's just a game. It's just that it's so long ago and that like, yes, it's sad--
<v Emanuele Berry>并不是说这只是场比赛。只是它过去太久了，就像，是的，这很伤感——

00:55:07.350 --> 00:55:12.470
<v Bobby Berry>Oh, believe me. In my life, I'm a very blessed and happy man.
<v Bobby Berry>哦，相信我。在我的人生中，我是一个非常受祝福且快乐的人。

00:55:12.470 --> 00:55:21.700
<v Emanuele Berry>Well, that's it, though. That's exactly it. It just feels like this is such an insignificant thing to all of the great shit that you have going on in your life.
<v Emanuele Berry>好吧，这就是重点，虽然。这就是完全的重点。这感觉就像相对于你生活中发生的所有伟大的事情，这是一个微不足道的事情。

00:55:21.700 --> 00:55:22.760
<v Bobby Berry>Watch the language.
<v Bobby Berry>注意语言。

00:55:22.760 --> 00:55:24.490
<v Emanuele Berry>Sorry.
<v Emanuele Berry>抱歉。

00:55:24.490 --> 00:55:29.380
<v Sean Cole>My dad did point out one positive thing in the video that I couldn't have noticed.
<v Sean Cole>我爸爸确实在视频里指出了我没注意到的一个积极点。

00:55:29.380 --> 00:55:30.820
<v Bobby Berry>You know what I said to my coach?
<v Bobby Berry>你知道我对教练说了什么吗？

00:55:30.820 --> 00:55:31.510
<v Emanuele Berry>What did you say?
<v Emanuele Berry>你说了什么？

00:55:31.510 --> 00:55:36.080
<v Bobby Berry>I'm sorry, sir.
<v Bobby Berry>我说，对不起，先生。

00:55:36.080 --> 00:55:38.060
<v Emanuele Berry>What were you sorry for?
<v Emanuele Berry>你对什么道歉？

00:55:38.060 --> 00:55:46.500
<v Bobby Berry>Losing the game. Now I gotta go. I never told anybody what I said to my coach.
<v Bobby Berry>输掉比赛。好了，我得走了。我从没告诉过任何人我对教练说了什么。

00:55:46.500 --> 00:55:49.720
<v Emanuele Berry>What did he say back?
<v Emanuele Berry>他回了什么？

00:55:49.720 --> 00:55:52.490
<v Bobby Berry>No, you played your ass off.
<v Bobby Berry>不，你拼尽全力了。

00:55:52.490 --> 00:56:08.090
<v Emanuele Berry>At this point, we've been talking for close to an hour. And I realized what I'm doing isn't working. I've been keeping things positive, trying to make my dad see something else-- sugar coating it. And you know what I hate? I hate when people sugar coat things.
<v Emanuele Berry>这时候，我们已经聊了快一个小时了。我意识到我在做的事没起作用。我一直保持积极，试图让我爸爸看到别的东西——粉饰它。你知道我讨厌什么吗？我讨厌人们粉饰事情。

00:56:08.090 --> 00:56:34.220
<v Emanuele Berry>The truth was, he was right. He didn't play well. That dunk-- he really did pass the ball over the rim, instead of just dropping it in. After that, he only scored three points. He played exactly the way he told me not to play for most of my basketball career, hanging out around the basket, hands down. He missed easy put backs. He did rebound well, but without him as a threat offensively, his team suffered.
<v Emanuele Berry>事实是，他是对的。他没打好。那次扣篮——他确实把球传过了篮圈，而不是直接投进。那之后，他只得了三分。他在我大部分篮球生涯中扮演了他告诉我不该扮演的角色，在篮筐周围闲逛，垂手。他投失了简单的补篮。他确实抢篮板不错，但没有他作为进攻威胁，他的球队遭受了打击。

00:56:34.220 --> 00:56:47.100
<v Emanuele Berry>I think he's absolutely right. If he'd played better, they would have won. Maybe what he needed wasn't to see himself differently. What he needed was for someone to see him just the way he is.
<v Emanuele Berry>我认为他绝对是对的。如果他打得更好，他们就会赢。也许他需要的不是以不同的方式看待自己。他需要的是有人能像他现在的样子看待他。

00:56:47.100 --> 00:56:50.400
<v Emanuele Berry>I mean, to be frank, it was not a great game for you.
<v Emanuele Berry>我的意思是，坦白说，那场比赛你打得并不好。

00:56:50.400 --> 00:56:52.040
<v Bobby Berry>It wasn't a great-- it was a horrible game for me.
<v Bobby Berry>那不是一场好——那对我来说是一场可怕的比赛。

00:56:52.040 --> 00:56:59.090
<v Emanuele Berry>But I wanted you to also see yourself play basketball. And I think I was hoping that it would be different than you imagined.
<v Emanuele Berry>但我也想让你看看自己打篮球。我想我当时是希望它会和你想象的不同。

00:56:59.090 --> 00:57:00.970
<v Bobby Berry>Why would you think that?
<v Bobby Berry>为什么你会那样想？

00:57:00.970 --> 00:57:08.780
<v Emanuele Berry>Because I always imagined that I played like shit. [LAUGHS] And I like to think I don't look that bad on tape.
<v Emanuele Berry>因为我总是想象我打得像屎一样。[笑] 我喜欢认为我在录像带里看起来没那么糟。

00:57:08.780 --> 00:57:11.770
<v Bobby Berry>Well, you see?
<v Bobby Berry>好吧，你看到了吗？

00:57:11.770 --> 00:57:31.470
<v Emanuele Berry>We chatted a little longer, my dad looking drained-- I think a little sad. It was late, and the Raptors were about to play the Bucks. So I left my dad to watch his game. I spent the evening pretending to read, but really, I was worried about what I just did. The next morning, my dad told me he had something he wanted to say.
<v Emanuele Berry>我们聊了一会儿，我爸爸看起来精疲力尽——我想有点伤心。天晚了，猛龙队正要打雄鹿队。所以我留我爸爸看他的比赛。我花了一晚上假装读书，但实际上，我担心我刚做的事。第二天早上，我爸爸告诉我他有话要说。

00:57:31.470 --> 00:58:06.020
<v Bobby Berry>You know, I actually felt a sense of relief after watching the game with you. I don't think I would've watched it, to tell you the truth. So getting through that with someone that you care and for them to sit there, and watch, and just be brutally honest, like you said, that I played like shit-- excuse my language. But those things are important.
<v Bobby Berry>你知道，和你一起看比赛后，我其实感到了一种解脱感。说实话，我不认为我会看它。所以和一个你在乎的人经历那个过程，让他们坐在那里，看着，并且就像你说的 brutally 诚实，我打得像屎一样——请原谅我的语言。但那些事情很重要。

00:58:06.020 --> 00:58:24.680
<v Emanuele Berry>And that's what I wanted, to talk to my dad about the important things. And since I started this conversation, we've been doing that more and more. We've talked about his childhood in Mississippi, about his health, like how dialysis is so depleting, and about his own parents and how he sees them.
<v Emanuele Berry>而那正是我想做的，和我的爸爸谈谈重要的事情。自从我开始这个对话，我们一直在做这件事。我们聊了他的童年、关于他的健康，就像透析是多么消耗体力，还有关于他的父母，以及他如何看待他们。

00:58:24.680 --> 00:58:39.780
<v Emanuele Berry>Our conversations are not always this deep. But you know what they're not always about? They're not always about basketball.
<v Emanuele Berry>我们的对话并不总是这么深刻。但你知道它们不总是什么吗？它们并不总是在谈论篮球。

00:58:39.780 --> 00:59:07.330
<v Sean Cole>Emanuele Berry is one of the producers of our show. A version of this story appeared on The Nod, a podcast that tells stories about black culture that you won't hear anywhere else. Like, LeVar Burton discussing the love life of black Star Trek characters. You can find The Nod wherever you get your podcasts.
<v Sean Cole>埃马努埃莱·贝里是我们节目的制作人之一。这个故事的一个版本出现在《The Nod》上，这是一个讲述你在其他地方听不到的黑人文化故事的播客。比如，勒瓦尔·伯顿讨论《星际迷航》中黑人角色的爱情生活。你可以在任何你获取播客的地方找到《The Nod》。

00:59:07.330 --> 00:59:30.670
<v Sean Cole>Our program was produced today by Lina Misitzis and Nadia Reiman. Our staff includes Bim Adewunmi, Elna Baker, Emanuele Berry, Ben Calhoun, Zoe Chace, Dana Chivvis, Aviva DeKornfeld, Neil Drumming, [? Hillary ?] [? Elkins, ?] [? Damien ?] [? Grave, ?] [? Michelle ?] [? Harris, ?] Seth Lind, Miki Meek, Stowe Nelson, [? Katherine ?] [? Raimondo, ?] Robyn Semien, Christopher Swetala, Matt Tierney, and Nancy Updike. Our managing editor is Diane Wu. Executive editor, David Kestenbaum.
<v Sean Cole>我们的节目今天由Lina Misitzis和Nadia Reiman制作。我们的员工包括Bim Adewunmi、Elna Baker、Emanuele Berry、Ben Calhoun、Zoe Chace、Dana Chivvis、Aviva DeKornfeld、Neil Drumming、[? Hillary ?] [? Elkins, ?] [? Damien ?] [? Grave, ?] [? Michelle ?] [? Harris, ?] Seth Lind、Miki Meek、Stowe Nelson, [? Katherine ?] [? Raimondo, ?] Robyn Semien, Christopher Swetala, Matt Tierney, 和 Nancy Updike。我们的主编是Diane Wu。执行主编David Kestenbaum。

00:59:30.670 --> 00:59:51.310
<v Sean Cole>Special thanks today to Dr. Cindy Cisneros-McGilvery, Jayson Haedrich, Rob Howes, Trevar Cushing, Tyler Rickstrew, Aurelie Hagen, Farley Chase, Eileen Berry, Tony Daniels, Jorge Just, and Sam Greenspan. Our website, ThisAmericanLife.org, where you can stream our archive of over 600 episodes for absolutely free-- ThisAmericanLife.org.
